			"id": "s2q8UJEUlCQZJI1FP",
			"name": "Theology",
			"reference": "B226",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Ecclesiarchy's dogma, liturgy, saint-cults and the countless local rites of Imperial Cult worship, from a hab-block shrine's litanies to a Cardinal-Astra's sermons. Depicted throughout Black Library fiction (Ciaphas Cain, Gaunt's Ghosts, the Eisenhorn/Ravenor books) as the working theology every Imperial citizen absorbs in some form.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Theology (B226), specialised as it already allows.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Knowledge",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"specialization": "Imperial Creed",
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"defaults": [
				{
					"type": "iq",
					"modifier": -6
				}
			],
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "ssRBeQsaHKwhreowu",
			"name": "Theology",
			"reference": "B226",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Cult of the Machine God: the Motive Force catechisms, the binary liturgies, the theology that says a machine's spirit must be placated, not merely fixed. Framework note: this is the Mechanicus's *faith*, distinct from the technical skill of maintaining machines (Engineer / Mechanic / Armoury), matching how Black Library depicts Tech-Priests as both engineers and priests of a religion.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Theology (B226) as a separate specialisation from Theology (Imperial Creed); the two cults' dogmas do not cross-default.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Knowledge",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"specialization": "Cult Mechanicus",
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"defaults": [
				{
					"type": "iq",
					"modifier": -6
				}
			],
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "sz5W-vey8_03vLMB9",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"reference": "B199",
			"local_notes": "Lore: What the Inquisition and the more paranoid chaplains know of daemonic nature, names, and countermeasures: pict-evidence, interrogation transcripts and forbidden grimoires rather than fieldcraft. Widely depicted as dangerous knowledge in the Eisenhorn/Ravenor and Gaunt's Ghosts novels; Dark Heresy/Only War use an equivalent Forbidden Lore (Daemonology) skill for calibration.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Hidden Lore (B199), specialisation per framework.md. Hidden Lore is IQ/Average with no default in the Basic Set, so none is listed here or on the other Hidden Lore specialisations.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Knowledge",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"specialization": "Daemons",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "sB-pd2vkGwm7RzU6m",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"reference": "B199",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Cross-referenced xenology from an Inquisitorial or Departmento Munitorum angle: what a given alien species is, not how to fight it (that's Expert Skill (Xenology) or Tactics). Covers everything from ork biology to eldar craftworld politics as known to Imperial intelligence, which is often wrong or incomplete by design.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Hidden Lore (B199).",
			"tags": [
