		{
			"id": "sw2AL6F2vHeU_G3G5",
			"name": "Navigation",
			"reference": "B211",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Charting a course through the Immaterium by the light of the Astronomican, correcting for warp storms and translation drift. In practice this is inseparable from the Navigator Houses' mutant third eye; without it the skill cannot be used at all (see framework.md, \"Skills\"). A ship's Navigator plots by this skill; the Warp-jump itself is the Navigator's psychic gift, not the roll.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Navigation (Hyperspace) (B211) renamed per framework.md. No default given: unlike terrestrial navigation, nothing else sensibly defaults into it, and GMs should restrict purchase to characters with the Navigator racial trait (handled elsewhere).",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Knowledge",
				"Imperium",
				"Restricted"
			],
			"specialization": "Warp",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 1
		},
