		{
			"id": "s4-7mLeU75Ku1R3dm",
			"name": "Savoir-Faire",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Ecclesiarchy protocol: forms of address for Cardinals, Confessors and Canonesses, precedence between Orders of the Adepta Sororitas, and the rites of a shrine world's court. Not attested in fiction as a named \"skill\", but the Ecclesiarchy is repeatedly shown (Sisters of Battle novels, Black Library's Sabbat Worlds material) to have as rigid a court culture as any noble house or general staff.\n\nDesign: New specialisation of Basic Set Savoir-Faire (B218), by direct analogy with the existing Military and High Society specialisations — same skill, same difficulty, applied to a third hierarchy the game needs and the catalogue doesn't name.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
