		{
			"id": "s6tIOW7euY-PojrXF",
			"name": "Cryptography",
			"reference": "B186",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Breaking (or setting) the rotating cant-ciphers Inquisitorial cells use to keep acolyte reports and warrant chains secret from each other as much as from heretics — Inquisitors are famously as suspicious of their own kind as of their prey (Eisenhorn, Ravenor).\n\nDesign: Basic Set Cryptography (B186), specialised; keeps the Basic Set default of Mathematics (Cryptology)-5, listed explicitly because GCS applies only the defaults written in the entry.",
